  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The diagnostic gate is undefined: specify cohort size, age bins, isolation threshold, random-control repetitions, effect threshold, and uncertainty. Greater sensitivity to isolated events does not establish that their influence harms accuracy.",
    "Deletion changes both history content and positional embeddings. Position-preserving masking and compacted deletion need separate controls, with explicit final-target alignment and exclusion of future interactions.",
    "The consistency loss lacks candidate count and sampling distribution, temperature, weight grid, reduction, dropout handling, and scheduling. A detached clean prediction can preserve existing errors; stability alone does not demonstrate improvement.",
    "Compare targeted deletion consistency with random-deletion consistency and a simple recency baseline under equal search budgets. Otherwise, improvements cannot be attributed to semantic targeting. Define TF–IDF settings, missing-text handling, and duplicate-item treatment.",
    "The report needs a concrete GPU-time allocation, checkpoint-selection rule, and stopping policy. Repeated validation selection can overfit 200 users per category; paired intervals do not account for search bias. Explicitly retain full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for the twenty training users.",
    "Originality 5/10 and difficulty 4/10 remain provisional without comparison to existing sequential-recommendation augmentation and consistency methods. Potential 7/10 is speculative because no diagnostic effect or accuracy gain has been measured, and the supplied references have not been independently verified."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Assess novelty and identify established loss designs and necessary controls.",
      "query": "Sequential recommendation history deletion augmentation consistency regularization SASRec: compare CL4SRec, CoSeRec, and DuoRec with semantic-isolation-targeted deletion and detached clean-to-augmented KL distillation. What losses, false-invariance risks, and random-augmentation ablations are documented?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve whether the proposed diagnostic measures harmful event dependence or positional artifacts.",
      "query": "SASRec counterfactual history deletion diagnostics positional embedding confounding: how can compacted deletion, position-preserving masking, age-matched random deletion, and fixed-last-item controls distinguish event-content dependence from sequence-length and position effects, and how are these effects linked to next-item ranking accuracy?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Improve reproducibility and guard against validation-driven shortcut selection.",
      "query": "Recommender-system hyperparameter search with small fixed validation cohorts: methods for controlling adaptive validation overfitting, paired HR@10 uncertainty, and equal-compute comparison of augmentation baselines when selecting models across multiple datasets using macro-average sampled ranking metrics."
    }
  ]
}
